  "result": "I implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 10 tests next to the existing ones in `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes: 12 tests, 0 failed.\n\nIt handles each rule like this:\n- **Diacritics:** `đ` and `Đ` are mapped to `d`. The text is then split into base letters and accent marks, and the marks are dropped.\n- **Lowercase and hyphens:** the text is lowercased, and each run of characters outside a-z and 0-9 becomes one hyphen. Hyphens at the start and end are trimmed.\n- **Length:** the slug is cut to 50 characters, then any hyphen left at the end of the cut is removed.\n\n`null` and `undefined` input return an empty string, which you didn't ask for. I added it so those inputs don't throw.\n\nThe tests cover basic hyphenation, Vietnamese and other Latin accents, `đ`/`Đ`, runs of symbols, trimming, empty and symbol-only input, and the 50-character cut. They check both a cut that lands on a hyphen and a slug that ends on a letter at exactly 50.",
